        "original_id": "8b0fd981-1a8c-521d-bd4b-84c6f47581a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John O'Hara, Rabindranath Tagore, Elizabeth Appleton\n- Roles: writer, polymath\n- Works: Elizabeth Appleton\n- Concepts: social realism, social status and manners, Contextual Modernism, Bengali literature, Bengali music, Indian art\n\nFacts:\n- Rabindranath Tagore was a Bengali polymath who reshaped Bengali literature and music, as well as Indian art through Contextual Modernism, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.\n- Rabindranath Tagore lived from 7 May 1861 to 7 August 1941 and was also known by the sobriquet Gurudev.\n- John Henry O'Hara lived from January 31, 1905 to April 11, 1970 and was an American writer.\n- John O'Hara was best remembered as a keen observer of social status and manners in early to mid 20th century America and as a leading depicter of social realism among his contemporaries.\n- Elizabeth Appleton is a novel by John O'Hara that was first published in 1963.",
